    "findings": [
      "Enum construct/tag/payload lowering created private scratch allocas in branch and loop blocks. LLVM did not eliminate that storage effectively. Hoisting only these nonescaping allocations to the entry block enables scalar replacement without changing enum layout, conditional writes or checks.",
      "The compiler fix removes measured local-memory sectors from 12389088 to zero. These were enum scratch stores, not register spills: spilling counters are zero in all variants.",
      "Descriptor computation outside elected-lane branches further reduces executed instructions. All eight MMA issues and the commit remain singly elected; repeated full-mask elections preserve the same leader.",
      "All variants are shared-memory occupancy limited to one CTA per SM with 74 resident clusters. The fix does not change occupancy.",
      "The hottest long-scoreboard samples are predicate consumers after acc_full waits: the epilogue waits for MMA completion. They do not establish that CCTL cache invalidation is the root cause.",
      "Strengthening the reference waits to cluster acquire barely changes fixed-clock duration (1.133056ms to 1.134432ms). Rust synchronization scope was retained.",
      "No-bias specialization reduces arithmetic but did not improve the fixed-clock profile, so it was discarded.",
      "The normal three-run comparison is effectively level; the controlled profile retains a 2.44 percent Rust duration overhead. Remaining instruction/control differences are not fully eliminated."
    ]
  }
}
